## Reproduced defect

At PR #84 head `eab900b02d1652884bdde10f12499340005cd4ed`, an ordinary loop can consume promotion capacity retained by a meta programme simply by spelling the same approval as `RL-APPROVAL` or `approval` instead of `rl-approval`. The SDK resolves all three to the same Decision, but the new retained-capacity accounting compares the raw approval string with the canonical identity stored in reservations.

This is additional evidence beyond the resolved [promotion-time capacity review](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/84#discussion_r4307244372): the existing concurrent regression uses the canonical approval spelling throughout.

## Goal and source evidence

- The accepted [meta feature](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/blob/eab900b02d1652884bdde10f12499340005cd4ed/.agents/pm/features/pm-rl-meta.toon) requires fail-closed promotion and idempotent accounting. The [current design](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/blob/eab900b02d1652884bdde10f12499340005cd4ed/docs/meta-recursive.md#L283-L301) says every promotion preserves unconsumed meta headroom under the shared writer lock
- [metaReservations](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/blob/eab900b02d1652884bdde10f12499340005cd4ed/meta.ts#L119-L131) filters with `record.approval === approval`; `reserveMeta` persists the SDK-resolved approval identity
- [promoteGenerationCore](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/blob/eab900b02d1652884bdde10f12499340005cd4ed/index.ts#L2461-L2468) passes its uncanonicalized approval input to the retained-capacity helper. Reading the approval successfully does not replace that input with `item.id`
- The same raw identity is also used in [consumed-promotion comparison](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/blob/eab900b02d1652884bdde10f12499340005cd4ed/index.ts#L1970-L1995), so resolving only reservation matching would leave inconsistent accounting for persisted alias spellings
- The pinned SDK `2026.10.13` already [lowercases IDs and supplies the workspace prefix](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/828edf4ae71d27c28a103ca05cec87366d88a5fd/src/core/item/id.ts#L37-L53); its [item lookup](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/828edf4ae71d27c28a103ca05cec87366d88a5fd/src/core/store/item-store.ts#L128-L150) applies those normalizers. This is static corroboration of the alias contract, not a claim that the end-to-end reproduction ran on that pin

## Sanitized reproduction

The following uses only the repository's synthetic committed-history fixture and ordinary numerical bandit loop. Save as `test/review-approval-alias.test.ts` in a disposable checkout of the tested commit and run `node --test test/review-approval-alias.test.ts`.

```ts
import assert from "node:assert/strict";
import { readFileSync } from "node:fs";
import { test } from "node:test";
import { runRlMeta, runRlLoop, type JsonValue } from "../index.ts";
import { retainedMetaPromotionHeadroom } from "../meta.ts";
import { metaWorkspace, metaConfig, metaSpec } from "./fixtures/meta-workspace.ts";

test("approval aliases preserve reserved promotion capacity", async () => {
  const w = await metaWorkspace();
  const alias = w.approval.toUpperCase(); // Also reproduced with "approval"
  assert.equal((await w.client.get(alias)).item.id, w.approval);
  await w.client.update(w.approval, {
    body: "```json\n" + JSON.stringify({ ...metaSpec, permitted_promotions: 4 }) + "\n```",
  });
  await assert.rejects(runRlMeta(w.client, w.coordinates, {
    id: "reserved", config: { ...metaConfig, meta_generations: 1, candidates: 1 },
    dataset: w.dataset, approval: w.approval, proposer: "seeded",
    onStep(key) { if (key === "programme") throw new Error("capacity held"); },
  }), /capacity held/);
  assert.equal(await retainedMetaPromotionHeadroom(w.client, w.approval, []), 4);
  const raw = JSON.parse(readFileSync(
    new URL("../examples/loop-bandit.json", import.meta.url), "utf8",
  )) as Record<string, JsonValue>;
  const report = await runRlLoop(w.client, w.coordinates, {
    id: "ordinary-alias", config: { ...raw, max_generations: 1 }, approval: alias,
  });
  assert.equal(report.promoted, 0, "all four slots are reserved");
});
```

Observed independently in fresh synthetic workspaces:
- Canonical `rl-approval` control: retained headroom 4, `promotion_refused`, 0 promoted; **1/1 passes**
- Uppercase `RL-APPROVAL`: SDK resolves `rl-approval`, helper returns headroom 0, `generation_limit`, 1 promoted; **0/1 passes**, assertion `1 !== 0`
- Short `approval`: same canonical resolution, headroom 0 and 1 promotion; **0/1 passes**, assertion `1 !== 0`

Expected: all equivalent spellings identify one approval budget; with all four slots reserved, an ordinary promotion is refused. Actual: one ordinary promotion succeeds beside four still-retained slots under a four-slot approval.

Impact: the shared-approval capacity guarantee depends on caller spelling and can be bypassed through the public SDK loop input. This establishes reserved-capacity oversubscription. No claim is made here about an additional live-provider run or a particular eventual total after resuming the owner.

## Verification limits

Reproduced directly from the named production sources on Node **24.19.0** with the already-available SDK **2026.10.18**. Repository pin is **2026.10.13** and hosted CI uses Node 22/26; no pinned-runtime full-suite certification is claimed. The pinned SDK alias behavior above was inspected statically.

Nine unchanged focused regressions at the tested head pass **9/9**, including ordinary concurrent promotions, shared headroom, interrupted retained-capacity replay, canonical reservation lookup, classified refusals, excluded-source case folding and packaged receipts. The new alias tests fail while changing only their approval spelling to the canonical ID passes.

Tests ran in disposable copies with isolated HOME/config/tmp, telemetry disabled, network/fetch and remote Git blocked, and only inspected synthetic fixture/local trainer processes allowed. No provider inference, live datasets, dependency changes, merge, release or deployment was performed. Exact-head CI run [39133504297](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/39133504297) was still running at filing preparation; historical 622-test results are not evidence for this head.

## Acceptance / regression criteria

1. Resolve and validate approval references to one canonical SDK item identity before reservation matching, consumed-promotion accounting and new promotion persistence; preserve fail-closed behavior if that identity cannot be established
2. Cover full canonical, uppercase and short-ID references against the same Decision, including mixed spellings across ordinary/manual and meta flows
3. With all capacity reserved, each alias must refuse ordinary promotion; with one free slot, concurrent mixed-alias callers must consume at most that one slot
4. Account safely for existing persisted approval aliases rather than treating their promotions as a fresh budget
5. Preserve the canonical owning-inner-generation exemption, atomic writer-lock checks, owner resume and terminal replay without extra charges
6. Run the new tests on pinned SDK 2026.10.13 and the unchanged npm/Bun release gates; retain a behavior-only revert proof

Deduplication checked all 84 existing issue/PR entries across open and closed states, all nine current PR review threads, and all 89 canonical PM records at the tested head. The programme-ID case-folding fix and the resolved general retained-capacity finding do not cover this approval-reference mismatch.


